  <prompt>Deliver the written contract-lock note to messaging-communication-app-r3 confirming the shipped communication-arrived trigger, envelope, consumer API, and degrade semantics — the formal answer their task 045's P1 gate is blocked on.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Precise technical writer — this note is read by a different project team as an authoritative contract; cite exact shipped file paths and API shapes, not paraphrases.</role>

  <goal>A contract-lock note exists at messaging-communication-app-r3's notes directory (the sibling worktree at C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/) confirming, with citations to the ACTUAL shipped code from tasks 013/020/021/022/024: (1) trigger = persistence, all channels, capture and send identically; (2) the spine emits, R3 consumes only — R3 must NOT wire its own communication-arrived producer; (3) the exact envelope shape (kind, communicationId, threadId, channel, direction, senderDisplay, optional privacy-gated snippet, badgeDelta); (4) the consumer API — the shared subscriber library's public contract (task 021) plus the pending/poll fallback endpoint (task 022); (5) degrade semantics (ADR-032 null-object — SignalR off falls back to the poll endpoint). The note formalizes R3's existing pre-implementation alignment note and unblocks their task 045.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec FR-19. R3 already has a PRE-implementation alignment note on file (C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/notification-spine-contract-alignment.md, dated 2026-07-20) recording their unresolved questions and this project's design-time answers. This task delivers the POST-implementation FORMAL lock — citing the actual shipped code (not the design-time promise) — so R3's task 045 can move from "blocked" to "verify-only" per that alignment note's own text ("Task 045's step 2... should be reconciled at P1 to 'verify the spine's emit fires'... Task 045 stays blocked until the spine's spec formalizes the above; this note is the design-level confirmation its escalation trigger asks for." — this task is the FOLLOW-UP formal confirmation once code has shipped).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/notification-spine-contract-alignment.md</file>
