  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the actual shipped shapes from tasks 013 (envelope types), 020 (negotiate endpoint + delivery entrypoint), 021 (subscriber library public API / README), 022 (pending endpoint), and 024 (communication-arrived producer trigger points) — verify each against code, not against this project's spec/plan promises.</step>
    <step order="2">Read R3's existing pre-implementation alignment note (C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/notification-spine-contract-alignment.md) to match its structure and answer its open items with confirmed, cited facts.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the contract-lock note covering: trigger=persistence (cite the exact persist call sites task 024 wired), spine-emits/R3-consumes (explicit MUST NOT), the envelope shape (cite task 013's types), the consumer API (cite task 021's library README + task 022's endpoint route), and degrade semantics (cite the ADR-032 null-object path).</step>
    <step order="4">Deliver the note to C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/notification-spine-contract-lock.md.</step>
    <step order="5">Mirror a copy into this project's own notes/handoffs/ for local traceability.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set task 025 to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of tasks 013/020/021/022/024's shipped shape materially contradicts what R3's existing alignment note assumed (e.g. a different envelope field set, a different endpoint route), STOP and flag the discrepancy explicitly in the note rather than quietly reconciling it — R3's task 045 needs to know if their assumption was wrong, not just the corrected answer.</trigger>
