  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the contract-lock note is read, when checked against task 024's shipped code, then its trigger description (persistence, all channels, capture+send identically) matches the actual wired call sites — not a paraphrase of the design-time spec.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the note states the consumer API, when checked against task 021's library and task 022's endpoint, then the cited method names / route / envelope fields match the shipped code exactly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the note is reviewed, when checked for the ownership statement, then it explicitly states R3 MUST NOT wire its own communication-arrived producer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the note is delivered, when its location is checked, then it exists at C:/code_files/spaarke-wt-messaging-communication-app-r3/projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/notification-spine-contract-lock.md (R3's own notes directory, not only this project's).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given degrade semantics are described, when checked against task 022's endpoint and the ADR-032 null-object pattern, then the note correctly states that SignalR-off falls back to the poll endpoint with no signal loss.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

